AB  - A suitable medium,95% wheat bran +5% maize flour + 5% soybean powder,was chosen for mass production of Beauveria bassiana for solid-state fermentation,and the spore count of primary product was up to 244.7×10~(8) conidia per gram.The optimal conditions for solid-state fermentation in a 25m~(3) solid fermentator were as followings.Initial water content of the medium was 60%--65%.The best aeration ratio was: 0 in first 12h,1:2 in 12--48h and 1:1 after 48h.In order to emit heat released by substantial growth of mycelium, it was necessary to control the temperature from 12h to 48±8h. As to the desiccating process, the optimal condition was with dried air at normal temperature to keep conidia viable.
