AB  - The invention provides a constructing method of bio-control fungi with reinforced stress resisting property, which comprises the following steps: (1) relevant genes for stress resistance are obtained, and are metallothionein genes or thioredoxin genes (2) a binary carrier of the metallothionein genes or the thioredoxin genes is constructed and (3) the binary carrier constructed is transferred to the biocontrol fungi, thus obtaining recombined bio-control fungi. The invention also provides a beauveria bassiana strain with reinforced stress resisting property, which utilizes the genetic transformation technology to shift fungal expression plasmids to the bio-control fungi, thus obtaining a recombined strain for the constitutive expression of the metallothionein genes or the thioredoxin genes the tolerance of the bio-control fungi is reinforced by removing thalli free radicals and restoring the activity of stress injured protein. The two plants of bio-control fungi obtained have higher heat resisting performance and radiation resisting property.
