AB  - A new centrosymmetric cyclohexapeptide, aspersymmetide A (<b>1</b>), together with a known peptide, asperphenamate (<b>2</b>), was isolated from the fungus <i>Aspergillus versicolor</i> isolated from a gorgonian coral <i>Carijoa</i> sp., collected from the South China Sea. The chemical structure of <b>1</b> was elucidated by analyzing its NMR spectroscopy and MS spectrometry data, and the absolute configurations of the amino acids of <b>1</b> were determined by Marfey's method and UPLC-MS analysis of the hydrolysate. Aspersymmetide A (<b>1</b>) represents the first example of marine-derived centrosymmetric cyclohexapeptide. Moreover, <b>1</b> exhibited weak cytotoxicity against NCI-H292 and A431 cell lines at the concentration of 10 μM.
