AB  - This invention relates to the biologic control of plagues, specifically, with a selection method of virulent fungi regarding their force to attack insects. The advantages of the present invention reside in a rapid and low cost methodology for isolating Beauveria bassiana mutants, which are enhanced regarding their virulence against insects such as the grasshopper [Sphenarium purpurascens] preventing excessive damages in the DNA of the selected fungi due to their virulence and that yields to the max the mutating material, preventing the destruction of too many microorganisms during the process. The method consists of: a) determining the minimum inhibiting concentration of 2DG for the wild strain b) determining the mortality response against UV light (% of mortality regarding irradiating time) c) irradiating with UV light, at the intensity determined in step b, a spores suspension of the wild stain Bb22 selecting the mutants using a culture mean with a concentration of 2DG at the con centration determined in step a and d) confirming the sporulation phenotypes, qualitative secretion of proteases, chitinases and lipases.
