AB  - A method for reducing the toxicity of strychnos nux-vomica seeds by solid fermentation with medicinal fungi comprises the following steps of: activating and culturing schizophyllum commune, shiraia bambusicola, coriolus unicolor, cantharellus cibarius, beauveria bassiana and cordyceps cicadae for fermentation oven-drying strychnos nux-vomica seeds, pulverizing, soaking in water, and autoclaving respectively inoculating the above fungi on the treated strychnos nux-vomica seeds, performing solid fermentation under certain conditions, collecting respective fermentation product, and drying at low temperature to obtain medicinal fungal substances. The inventive method is simple and reasonable, and can obtain six medicinal fungal substances with reduced toxicity of strychnos nux-vomica seeds suitable for treatment purpose. The medicinal fungal substances have toxicity remarkably lower than that of strychnos nux-vomica seeds, have definite analgesic and antiphlogistic effects, and can keep the original main drug effect of Strychnos nux-vomica seed.
