AB  - In this paper, virulence of the solid products of the four fungal species (total 9 strains) as well as the mixture of the fungi and Bt (Bacillus thuringiensis) formulation to H. assulta larvae were tested. The results showed as follows: (1) Virulence of different fungal species and strains was various. Beauveria bassiana and Nomuraea rileyi had obvious controlling efficacy to H. assulta, and the former was prior to the latter. Virulence of the B. b strain 5S03 to H. assulta was highest, the LT_(50) for the 2nd instar larvae of H. assulta was about 6.10 days, adjusted death rate was 83.96 percent, and muscardine cadaver rate was 33.33 percent. (2) The controlling efficacy to H. assulta was enhanced when the strain 5S03 was mixed with Bt.
