AB  - Different characters of Beauveria bassiana (Bals.) Vuill. from various origins were observed and determined, three major groups were composed. The biological characters (group 1) were contributed by indexes as cultural characters, sporulation, colony growth rate and half conidia germination time (GT_(50)). The ecological characters (group 2) were composed by indexes as strain virulence, conidia rapid dis- and rehydration viability, ultraviolet radiation viability and bathing viability. The biochemical characters (group 3) were determined including indexes as oxalic acid content, and 5 enzyme productions, protease, chitinase, glucosidase, estrase isozyme and lipase. The major indexesd between different group were achieved by canonical analysis.
