AB  - The virulence of different entomogenous fungi on adult pine sawyers, Monochamus alternatus Hope was tested. The result showed that the virulence varied. Among them, Ma83, a Metarhizium anisopliae isolate, was the most virulent one. The mortality of the sawyers was up to 100% and the infection rate was 79%. LT_(50) was 5.24 days. Its LC_(50) on the adult sawyer was determined to be 1.38×10~(6) conidia per mL. The experiment was made to expose different parts of the sawyers to the fungal bands for infection. The infection increased and medium lethal time declined in an order of antenna, mouth part, leg and abdomen. Bb202-1 strain had higher virulence against adult sawyers in the forest.
