AB  - Virulence of the five fungal species (total 10 strains) to H.arigera larvae was tested by setting up different conidial deses and temperature conditions. The results showed as follow:(1)Virulence of differnt fungal species and strains were various. Beauveria bassiana and Nomuraea rileyi had obvious controlling to H.armigera, and the former is prior to the latter. Virulence of the B.b strain 5S03 to H. armigera was the highest, the LT_(50) for the 1st and 2nd instar larvae was about from 6.70 to 7.02 days, with adjusted death rates from 86.96 to 91.30 percent and muscardine cadaver rates from 20.00 to 36.67 percent.(2) The difference of virulence of the same strain was extremely obvious for different physiological condition and different of virulence of the same strain was extremely obvious for different physiologicl conditin and different instar larvae, the new ecdysial larvae were subject to injecting, the muscardine cadaver rate reached at 85.71 percent. The y oung instar larvae were more sensitive, and the difference reached at more than 35 percent for adjusted death rates and more than four days for LT_(50) compared with the old instar larvae. (3) the most suitable desity of 5S03 to control H.armigera was 7.8×10_(7) conidia/ml,and temperature was from 20 to 25℃.
