AB  - The insects Ostrinia rubililalis (Hubner), Tenebrio molitor L., Anthereaea pernyi Gnerin Meneville, Galleria mellonella, Plutella maculipennis Curtis, Heliothis armigera Butler, Aedes albopictus Skuse and Culex fatigaus Wiedemann were tested for the bioassay of products of the entomopathogenic fungus Beauveria bassiana. The results showed that A. albopictus and C.fatigaus were sensitive to the fungus products, other insects were tolerant to the fungus products. The LC_(50) of A. albupictus to the fungus powder was 8.83,7.06 and 8.8mg/ml respectively. The LC_(50) of C.fatigaus to the fungus powder was 20, 29,31mg/ml respectively. The CV of the LC_(50) of A.albopictus was less than 0.2, and that of C.fatigaus was more than 0.2. The larva of A.albopictus is suitable to be the index insect of the fungus products for bioassay.
