AB  - Nosema locustae Canning, Bacillus cereus Frankland and Frankland, Sporoethrix sp. were selected and applied to control cotton locust (Chondracris rosea rosea De Geer) and an infection rate over 77% was obtained. Beauveria bassiana, isolated from Anoplophora chinensis, was used to control Anoplophora chinensis and the infection rate was up to 77.8%. Steinernema feltiae, S. carpocapsae was used in the control of Anoplophora chinensis and the parasitized rate was over 90%. The results provided a scientific basis for the integrated control of the coastal Casuarina forest pess and diseases.
